-- Corpus sweep 2026-08-26: equipment-constrained programming, tempo /
-- technique modifiers, and Olympic lifting. 155 findings from 17 deep-read
-- batches over transcripts already on disk.
--
-- Adds a PROVENANCE column, and the reason is itself one of the findings:
-- the olympic synthesis reports that ~90% of that area comes from a single
-- channel whose owner has a commercial stake in the answer, and that every
-- "study" in it is a secondhand relay by that coach. Agreement inside one
-- voice is not corroboration. Without a source column, that caveat lives
-- only in a summary nobody queries.
--
-- `quantities` is jsonb and existing rows hold structured objects. These
-- findings arrived as prose, so each goes under a `note` key rather than
-- being parsed into a structure that was never extracted.
ALTER TABLE public.corpus_findings
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS source text;







